What is Included?

A complete Secured Promissory Note usually contains:
• Lender and borrower full names
• Loan principal amount
• Interest rate (if any)
• Repayment schedule or due date
• Detailed collateral description
• Default and seizure terms
• Late payment penalties
• Governing law clause
• Signatures of parties

What Does "Secured" Mean?

A Secured Promissory Note means the loan is backed by property pledged as collateral. If repayment is not made, the lender may recover value from that asset.

Secured vs Unsecured Promissory Note

Secured Promissory Note: backed by collateral
Unsecured Promissory Note: no collateral, based only on borrower promise

